solution:
1. Compute the length of the line segment $AM$:
   \begin{align*}
   AM &= \sqrt{(-5 - (-5))^2 + (5 - 1)^2} \\
   &= \sqrt{0 + 4^2} \\
   &= \sqrt{16} \\
   &= 4
   \end{align*}
2. Compute the length of the line segment $BI$:
   \begin{align*}
   BI &= \sqrt{(2 - 2)^2 + (6 - 2)^2} \\
   &= \sqrt{0 + 4^2} \\
   &= \sqrt{16} \\
   &= 4
   \end{align*}
3. Compute the length of the line segment $DE$:
   \begin{align*}
   DE &= \sqrt{(2 - 2)^2 + (-2 - (-6))^2} \\
   &= \sqrt{0 + 4^2} \\
   &= \sqrt{16} \\
   &= 4
   \end{align*}
4. Compute the length of the line segment $XT$:
   \begin{align*}
   XT &= \sqrt{(-6 - 5)^2 + (-3 - 6)^2} \\
   &= \sqrt{(-11)^2 + (-9)^2} \\
   &= \sqrt{121 + 81} \\
   &= \sqrt{202} \\
   &= 9
   \end{align*}
5. Compute the length of the line segment $RO$:
   \begin{align*}
   RO &= \sqrt{(-3 - (-3))^2 + (-6 - (-3))^2} \\
   &= \sqrt{0 + (-3)^2} \\
   &= \sqrt{9} \\
   &= 3
   \end{align*}
6. Compute the length of the line segment $US$:
   \begin{align*}
   US &= \sqrt{(5 - 5)^2 + (5 - 3)^2} \\
   &= \sqrt{0 + 2^2} \\
   &= \sqrt{4} \\
   &= 2
   \end{align*}
7. Compute the length of the line segment $LY$:
   \begin{align*}
   LY &= \sqrt{(8 - 3)^2 + (-5 - (-5))^2} \\
   &= \sqrt{5^2 + 0} \\
   &= \sqrt{25} \\
   &= 5
   \end{align*}
8. Sum the lengths of the line segments:
   \begin{align*}
   AM + BI + DE + XT + RO + US + LY &= 4 + 4 + 4 + 9 + 3 + 2 + 5 \\
   &= \boxed{31}
   \end{align*}

