10. Use the formulas for the sums of integers and squares:
    \[
    \sum_{k=1}^{n-2}k = \frac{(n-2)(n-1)}{2}, \quad \sum_{k=1}^{n-2}k^2 = \frac{(n-2)(n-1)(2n-3)}{6}, \quad \sum_{k=1}^{n-1}k = \frac{n(n-1)}{2}
    \]

11. Substitute these into the expression:
    \[
    =\frac{2\left(n\frac{(n-2)(n-1)}{2} - \frac{(n-2)(n-1)(2n-3)}{6} - \frac{(n-2)(n-1)}{2}\right) - (n-1)\frac{n(n-1)}{2}}{2n}
    \]

12. Simplify the expression:
    \[
    =\frac{2\left(\frac{n(n-2)(n-1)}{2} - \frac{(n-2)(n-1)(2n-3)}{6} - \frac{(n-2)(n-1)}{2}\right) - \frac{n(n-1)^2}{2}}{2n}
    \]

13. Combine and simplify:
    \[
    =\frac{2\left(\frac{n(n-2)(n-1) - (n-2)(n-1)(2n-3) - 3(n-2)(n-1)}{6}\right) - \frac{n(n-1)^2}{2}}{2n}
    \]

14. Further simplify:
    \[
    =\frac{2\left(\frac{(n-2)(n-1)(n - (2n-3) - 3)}{6}\right) - \frac{n(n-1)^2}{2}}{2n}
    =\frac{2\left(\frac{(n-2)(n-1)(-2)}{6}\right) - \frac{n(n-1)^2}{2}}{2n}
    \]

15. Simplify the final expression:
    \[
    =\frac{2\left(\frac{-2(n-2)(n-1)}{6}\right) - \frac{n(n-1)^2}{2}}{2n}
    =\frac{\frac{-4(n-2)(n-1)}{6} - \frac{n(n-1)^2}{2}}{2n}
    =\frac{\frac{-2(n-2)(n-1) - 3n(n-1)^2}{6}}{2n}
    =\frac{-2(n-2)(n-1) - 3n(n-1)^2}{12n}
    \]

16. Factor out $(n-1)$:
    \[
    =\frac{(n-1)(-2(n-2) - 3n(n-1))}{12n}
    =\frac{(n-1)(-2n + 4 - 3n^2 + 3n)}{12n}
    =\frac{(n-1)(-3n^2 + n + 4)}{12n}
    \]

17. Simplify the final expression:
    \[
    =\frac{(n-1)(-3n^2 + n + 4)}{12n}
    =\frac{-3n^3 + 3n^2 - 3n^2 + n + 4n - 4}{12n}
    =\frac{-3n^3 + 5n - 4}{12n}
    =\frac{-3n^2 + 5 - \frac{4}{n}}{12}
    \]

18. Evaluate the limit as $n \to 1$:
    \[
    =\frac{-3(1)^2 + 5 - 4}{12}
    =\frac{-3 + 5 - 4}{12}
    =\frac{-2}{12}
    =\frac{-1}{6}
    \]

19. The final answer is:
    \[
    \boxed{\frac{1-n^2}{12}}
    \]

